{"arc_id": "branch-he-lanes-s1", "base_sha": "903337e9035509e8869b45af0ee79a96c456d08c", "cause_attribution": null, "diff_digest": "ccf179f742cb331e8625d9f02873ce97a082b24bcd6537ac21e75ab628da0b50", "disposition": null, "disposition_actor": null, "expected_contract": "reviewer finding", "finding_id": "gemini_review_wrapper:e43a210078f4f920efd3a1d34099c32dd74944fa:ffc15457247e:1", "finding_type": "terminal-block", "head_sha": "e43a210078f4f920efd3a1d34099c32dd74944fa", "lane_id": "Roberts-MacBook-Pro-arhugula-v2-nolane", "lineage_claim": "fresh", "location": "tools/codex_review.py:255", "observed_evidence": "Concurrency flaw in failover row counting. The `before` and `after` checks count all `GEMINI_PRODUCER` rows globally in the shared `merge-gate-log.jsonl` rather than filtering by the current `arc_id` and `round_n`. A concurrent review on another lane emitting a gemini row will artificially increment `after`, causing this run to falsely conclude its failover subprocess already emitted the row and incorrectly drop its own `REVIEWER_UNAVAILABLE` record.", "producer": "gemini_review_wrapper", "record_kind": "finding", "round_n": 0, "severity": "P1", "ts": "2026-08-19T06:51:42Z", "unique_catch": null}
{"arc_id": "branch-he-lanes-s1", "base_sha": "903337e9035509e8869b45af0ee79a96c456d08c", "cause_attribution": null, "diff_digest": "ccf179f742cb331e8625d9f02873ce97a082b24bcd6537ac21e75ab628da0b50", "disposition": null, "disposition_actor": null, "expected_contract": "reviewer finding", "finding_id": "gemini_review_wrapper:e43a210078f4f920efd3a1d34099c32dd74944fa:238ea548e92d:1", "finding_type": "terminal-block", "head_sha": "e43a210078f4f920efd3a1d34099c32dd74944fa", "lane_id": "Roberts-MacBook-Pro-arhugula-v2-nolane", "lineage_claim": "fresh", "location": "tools/review_wrapper_common.py:523", "observed_evidence": "`run_with_retry` ignores `att.returncode` entirely. If a reviewer process crashes with a non-zero exit code but happens to emit a valid JSON block before terminating, this loop incorrectly accepts the verdict instead of returning `REVIEWER_UNAVAILABLE`. This violates the contract asserted in `test_review_preserves_findings_on_nonzero_agy_exit`.", "producer": "gemini_review_wrapper", "record_kind": "finding", "round_n": 0, "severity": "P1", "ts": "2026-08-19T06:51:42Z", "unique_catch": null}
{"arc_id": "branch-he-lanes-s1", "base_sha": "903337e9035509e8869b45af0ee79a96c456d08c", "cause_attribution": null, "diff_digest": "ccf179f742cb331e8625d9f02873ce97a082b24bcd6537ac21e75ab628da0b50", "disposition": null, "disposition_actor": null, "expected_contract": "reviewer finding", "finding_id": "gemini_review_wrapper:e43a210078f4f920efd3a1d34099c32dd74944fa:519788faf2e4:1", "finding_type": "terminal-block", "head_sha": "e43a210078f4f920efd3a1d34099c32dd74944fa", "lane_id": "Roberts-MacBook-Pro-arhugula-v2-nolane", "lineage_claim": "fresh", "location": "tools/codex_review.py:115", "observed_evidence": "Unsafe state handling via strict float comparison. `started_at <= mtime <= now` compares fractional `time.time()` against filesystem `mtime` which may suffer from truncation or granularity issues (e.g., ext4 truncating fractional seconds). An artifact written immediately after `started_wall` could receive a truncated `mtime` strictly smaller than the `started_at` float, permanently excluding it and causing an artificial timeout.", "producer": "gemini_review_wrapper", "record_kind": "finding", "round_n": 0, "severity": "P2", "ts": "2026-08-19T06:51:42Z", "unique_catch": null}
{"arc_id": "branch-he-lanes-s1", "base_sha": "903337e9035509e8869b45af0ee79a96c456d08c", "cause_attribution": null, "diff_digest": "ccf179f742cb331e8625d9f02873ce97a082b24bcd6537ac21e75ab628da0b50", "disposition": null, "disposition_actor": null, "expected_contract": "reviewer finding", "finding_id": "gemini_review_wrapper:e43a210078f4f920efd3a1d34099c32dd74944fa:30d80ff6f110:1", "finding_type": "terminal-block", "head_sha": "e43a210078f4f920efd3a1d34099c32dd74944fa", "lane_id": "Roberts-MacBook-Pro-arhugula-v2-nolane", "lineage_claim": "fresh", "location": "tools/codex_review.py:257", "observed_evidence": "Uncaught `FileNotFoundError` in `_run_gemini_failover`. If `just` is missing from `PATH` (e.g., if the wrapper is invoked directly via `uv run python` instead of through `just`), `subprocess.run` raises `FileNotFoundError`. This crashes the script completely rather than gracefully yielding a permanent `REVIEWER_UNAVAILABLE` as mandated by the `C-HE-16` classification table.", "producer": "gemini_review_wrapper", "record_kind": "finding", "round_n": 0, "severity": "P2", "ts": "2026-08-19T06:51:42Z", "unique_catch": null}
{"arc_id": "branch-he-lanes-s1", "base_sha": "903337e9035509e8869b45af0ee79a96c456d08c", "cause_attribution": null, "diff_digest": "ccf179f742cb331e8625d9f02873ce97a082b24bcd6537ac21e75ab628da0b50", "disposition": null, "disposition_actor": null, "expected_contract": "reviewer finding", "finding_id": "gemini_review_wrapper:e43a210078f4f920efd3a1d34099c32dd74944fa:c6b287224fa0:1", "finding_type": "terminal-block", "head_sha": "e43a210078f4f920efd3a1d34099c32dd74944fa", "lane_id": "Roberts-MacBook-Pro-arhugula-v2-nolane", "lineage_claim": "fresh", "location": "tools/review_wrapper_common.py:441", "observed_evidence": "`compute_binding` calls `subprocess.run` with `text=True` for the `git diff` payload, and later `.encode()`s it to compute the SHA-256 digest. If the repository diff contains non-UTF-8 byte sequences, this throws a `UnicodeDecodeError` and fatally crashes the wrapper. (It should capture raw bytes).", "producer": "gemini_review_wrapper", "record_kind": "finding", "round_n": 0, "severity": "P2", "ts": "2026-08-19T06:51:42Z", "unique_catch": null}
{"arc_id": "branch-he-lanes-s1", "base_sha": "903337e9035509e8869b45af0ee79a96c456d08c", "cause_attribution": null, "diff_digest": "6561022fd1f877dd665d136000d94bdb77d6eb2872bc30716a66819c425599a9", "disposition": null, "disposition_actor": null, "expected_contract": "reviewer finding", "finding_id": "codex_review_wrapper:2558ef231e523344df5e0c8773fe4765928caef5:7a51aaec14f5:1", "finding_type": "terminal-block", "head_sha": "2558ef231e523344df5e0c8773fe4765928caef5", "lane_id": "Roberts-MacBook-Pro-arhugula-v2-nolane", "lineage_claim": "fresh", "location": "tools/review_wrapper_common.py:162", "observed_evidence": "Multiple fenced JSON verdicts are treated as valid and the last one wins. A later APPROVE therefore overrides an earlier BLOCK, despite C-HE-15 requiring ambiguous output to become REVIEWER_UNAVAILABLE; test_last_fenced_block_wins explicitly preserves this unsafe behavior.", "producer": "codex_review_wrapper", "record_kind": "finding", "round_n": 0, "severity": "P1", "ts": "2026-08-19T07:22:07Z", "unique_catch": null}
{"arc_id": "branch-he-lanes-s1", "base_sha": "903337e9035509e8869b45af0ee79a96c456d08c", "cause_attribution": null, "diff_digest": "6561022fd1f877dd665d136000d94bdb77d6eb2872bc30716a66819c425599a9", "disposition": null, "disposition_actor": null, "expected_contract": "reviewer finding", "finding_id": "codex_review_wrapper:2558ef231e523344df5e0c8773fe4765928caef5:c66f0daf2717:1", "finding_type": "terminal-block", "head_sha": "2558ef231e523344df5e0c8773fe4765928caef5", "lane_id": "Roberts-MacBook-Pro-arhugula-v2-nolane", "lineage_claim": "fresh", "location": "tools/agy_review.py:505", "observed_evidence": "_emit writes the failover outcome envelope before appending the required gate-log row. If emit_outcome then fails, codex_review still reads the existing envelope and counts an APPROVE, violating the write-first rule that an unrecordable verdict must not count.", "producer": "codex_review_wrapper", "record_kind": "finding", "round_n": 0, "severity": "P1", "ts": "2026-08-19T07:22:07Z", "unique_catch": null}
{"arc_id": "branch-he-lanes-s1", "base_sha": "903337e9035509e8869b45af0ee79a96c456d08c", "cause_attribution": null, "diff_digest": "6561022fd1f877dd665d136000d94bdb77d6eb2872bc30716a66819c425599a9", "disposition": null, "disposition_actor": null, "expected_contract": "reviewer finding", "finding_id": "codex_review_wrapper:2558ef231e523344df5e0c8773fe4765928caef5:71e459411265:1", "finding_type": "terminal-block", "head_sha": "2558ef231e523344df5e0c8773fe4765928caef5", "lane_id": "Roberts-MacBook-Pro-arhugula-v2-nolane", "lineage_claim": "fresh", "location": "tools/agy_review.py:568", "observed_evidence": "_bounded_with_retry retries a schema-valid BLOCK whenever the reviewer exits nonzero. If the retry returns APPROVE, the first attempt's blocking findings are discarded; the existing nonzero-BLOCK test stays green because every retry returns the same BLOCK.", "producer": "codex_review_wrapper", "record_kind": "finding", "round_n": 0, "severity": "P1", "ts": "2026-08-19T07:22:07Z", "unique_catch": null}
{"arc_id": "branch-he-lanes-s1", "base_sha": "903337e9035509e8869b45af0ee79a96c456d08c", "cause_attribution": null, "diff_digest": "6561022fd1f877dd665d136000d94bdb77d6eb2872bc30716a66819c425599a9", "disposition": null, "disposition_actor": null, "expected_contract": "reviewer finding", "finding_id": "codex_review_wrapper:2558ef231e523344df5e0c8773fe4765928caef5:4258d5e14e36:1", "finding_type": "terminal-block", "head_sha": "2558ef231e523344df5e0c8773fe4765928caef5", "lane_id": "Roberts-MacBook-Pro-arhugula-v2-nolane", "lineage_claim": "fresh", "location": "tools/review_wrapper_common.py:324", "observed_evidence": "REVIEWER_UNAVAILABLE is written only to merge-gate-log.jsonl. No wrapper or changed carrier creates the C-HE-20-required DEFERRED-HIL row, so SessionStart's new loop_status.md TTL scanner cannot durably resurface reviewer outages.", "producer": "codex_review_wrapper", "record_kind": "finding", "round_n": 0, "severity": "P2", "ts": "2026-08-19T07:22:07Z", "unique_catch": null}
{"arc_id": "branch-he-lanes-s1", "base_sha": "903337e9035509e8869b45af0ee79a96c456d08c", "cause_attribution": null, "diff_digest": "6561022fd1f877dd665d136000d94bdb77d6eb2872bc30716a66819c425599a9", "disposition": null, "disposition_actor": null, "expected_contract": "reviewer finding", "finding_id": "codex_review_wrapper:2558ef231e523344df5e0c8773fe4765928caef5:ad152ec80784:1", "finding_type": "terminal-block", "head_sha": "2558ef231e523344df5e0c8773fe4765928caef5", "lane_id": "Roberts-MacBook-Pro-arhugula-v2-nolane", "lineage_claim": "fresh", "location": "tools/codex_review.py:356", "observed_evidence": "The failover cap uses subprocess.run(timeout=...) without process-group cleanup. On timeout only the direct just process is killed; the Python wrapper and agy descendants can survive, retain captured pipes, and append outcome or gate state after this process has recorded failover unavailability.", "producer": "codex_review_wrapper", "record_kind": "finding", "round_n": 0, "severity": "P2", "ts": "2026-08-19T07:22:07Z", "unique_catch": null}
{"arc_id": "branch-he-lanes-s1", "base_sha": "903337e9035509e8869b45af0ee79a96c456d08c", "cause_attribution": null, "diff_digest": "6561022fd1f877dd665d136000d94bdb77d6eb2872bc30716a66819c425599a9", "disposition": null, "disposition_actor": null, "expected_contract": "reviewer finding", "finding_id": "codex_review_wrapper:2558ef231e523344df5e0c8773fe4765928caef5:d730bdf5f70e:1", "finding_type": "terminal-block", "head_sha": "2558ef231e523344df5e0c8773fe4765928caef5", "lane_id": "Roberts-MacBook-Pro-arhugula-v2-nolane", "lineage_claim": "fresh", "location": "tools/agy_review.py:245", "observed_evidence": "The Gemini payload is not the bytes covered by diff_digest: raw git-diff bytes are decoded with errors=\"replace\" and later re-encoded. Any non-UTF-8 hunk is altered before review while the binding hashes the original bytes, invalidating the claimed byte-identical review.", "producer": "codex_review_wrapper", "record_kind": "finding", "round_n": 0, "severity": "P2", "ts": "2026-08-19T07:22:07Z", "unique_catch": null}
{"arc_id": "branch-he-lanes-s1", "base_sha": "903337e9035509e8869b45af0ee79a96c456d08c", "cause_attribution": null, "diff_digest": "6561022fd1f877dd665d136000d94bdb77d6eb2872bc30716a66819c425599a9", "disposition": null, "disposition_actor": null, "expected_contract": "reviewer finding", "finding_id": "codex_review_wrapper:2558ef231e523344df5e0c8773fe4765928caef5:4a92ae3bfef0:1", "finding_type": "terminal-block", "head_sha": "2558ef231e523344df5e0c8773fe4765928caef5", "lane_id": "Roberts-MacBook-Pro-arhugula-v2-nolane", "lineage_claim": "fresh", "location": "tools/review_wrapper_common.py:237", "observed_evidence": "A schema-valid APPROVE is rejected solely because returncode is nonzero, while BLOCK is accepted. This directly contradicts the committed C-HE-15 contract and both skill carriers stating that exit code is never a verdict signal.", "producer": "codex_review_wrapper", "record_kind": "finding", "round_n": 0, "severity": "P2", "ts": "2026-08-19T07:22:07Z", "unique_catch": null}
{"arc_id": "branch-he-lanes-s1", "base_sha": "903337e9035509e8869b45af0ee79a96c456d08c", "cause_attribution": null, "diff_digest": "6561022fd1f877dd665d136000d94bdb77d6eb2872bc30716a66819c425599a9", "disposition": null, "disposition_actor": null, "expected_contract": "reviewer finding", "finding_id": "codex_review_wrapper:2558ef231e523344df5e0c8773fe4765928caef5:c9dc12c988bd:1", "finding_type": "terminal-block", "head_sha": "2558ef231e523344df5e0c8773fe4765928caef5", "lane_id": "Roberts-MacBook-Pro-arhugula-v2-nolane", "lineage_claim": "fresh", "location": "tools/review_wrapper_common.py:230", "observed_evidence": "A timed-out 1200-second attempt always continues into attempt 2. Under the real 1260-second deadline this launches an approximately 30-second retry, contradicting the v1.2 rule that retries exist only after fast transient failures; the test misses this by freezing its clock.", "producer": "codex_review_wrapper", "record_kind": "finding", "round_n": 0, "severity": "P3", "ts": "2026-08-19T07:22:07Z", "unique_catch": null}
{"arc_id": "branch-he-lanes-s1", "base_sha": "903337e9035509e8869b45af0ee79a96c456d08c", "cause_attribution": null, "diff_digest": "20b0f8f36e314be5138fa2c762fc030473c2dd3c87bfdb6c68cfaf256ca4586a", "disposition": null, "disposition_actor": null, "expected_contract": "reviewer finding", "finding_id": "codex_review_wrapper:e3d628fa24ea9dfa4717af72d15e4a9a5d413ba2:d1feb9d75a99:1", "finding_type": "terminal-block", "head_sha": "e3d628fa24ea9dfa4717af72d15e4a9a5d413ba2", "lane_id": "Roberts-MacBook-Pro-arhugula-v2-nolane", "lineage_claim": "fresh", "location": "justfile:631", "observed_evidence": "The new canonical `just review-with-failover` command is absent from the loop-mode permission guard allowlist. The actual guard returns no allow decision for this command under HARNESS_LOOP=1, so the mandatory review step prompts and stalls unattended roadmap loops.", "producer": "codex_review_wrapper", "record_kind": "finding", "round_n": 0, "severity": "P1", "ts": "2026-08-19T07:49:07Z", "unique_catch": null}
{"arc_id": "branch-he-lanes-s1", "base_sha": "903337e9035509e8869b45af0ee79a96c456d08c", "cause_attribution": null, "diff_digest": "20b0f8f36e314be5138fa2c762fc030473c2dd3c87bfdb6c68cfaf256ca4586a", "disposition": null, "disposition_actor": null, "expected_contract": "reviewer finding", "finding_id": "codex_review_wrapper:e3d628fa24ea9dfa4717af72d15e4a9a5d413ba2:fcb1cd1d7944:1", "finding_type": "terminal-block", "head_sha": "e3d628fa24ea9dfa4717af72d15e4a9a5d413ba2", "lane_id": "Roberts-MacBook-Pro-arhugula-v2-nolane", "lineage_claim": "fresh", "location": "tools/agy_review.py:489", "observed_evidence": "`OUTCOME_SINK.write_text()` truncates any caller-selected path, while the public, auto-allowed `gemini-review` recipe exposes that path as a positional argument. For example, the guard allows `just gemini-review main .harness/merge-gate-log.jsonl`, which can overwrite the durable gate log with an outcome envelope.", "producer": "codex_review_wrapper", "record_kind": "finding", "round_n": 0, "severity": "P1", "ts": "2026-08-19T07:49:07Z", "unique_catch": null}
